                <pb facs="0614" n="586" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v20/pg586"/>

                <head>297. Telegram From the Mission to the United Nations to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d297-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>New York</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-09-25">September 25, 1962</date>,
                        midnight.</dateline></opener>
                <p>905. Congo. During Yost call on Bunche this afternoon latter described meeting
                    between Spaak and SYG on Congo at which it agreed that Tshombe unlikely implement reconciliation plan unless he forced
                    to do so. Bunche had suggested and others
                    agreed that only cut-off of UMHK payments to
                        Tshombe could force him to cooperate.
                    As result, Bunche had drafted and sent to
                        Gardiner cable setting forth this
                    view and submitting for Gardiner’s
                    comments following proposal: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>PriMin Adoula would send letter
                            to UMHK notifying it that he expected all
                                UMHK payments be made directly to
                            GOC.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>PriMin would have Congo Parliament pass legislation requiring that all
                            payments by mining companies be made directly to GOC.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>PriMin would send letter to Belgian Government asking it to assure
                                UMHK compliance with new law.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>SYG would send letter to appropriate
                                UN member states eliciting their help
                            in obtaining compliance with law.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>SYG would go to SC with request for approval his action and asking for
                            specific authority to guard UMHK
                            installations.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Bunche was very pessimistic over Tshombe’s attitude. Cited as two recent
                    indications of it the unreasonable line taken by Tshombe’s representative in military commission and deliberate
                    mining by Katangese of route traveled by Gurkha patrol. Said Katanga military
                    commission rep had demanded that UN evacuate
                    Elizabethville airfield. Charged that mine which killed Gurkhas had been touched
                    off when they were retracing route they had just successfully traversed.</p>
                <pb facs="0615" n="587" xml:id="pg587"/>
                <p>Bunche said he had asked SYG what he would do if plan failed. SYG had replied he would go to SC and ask for authority to withdraw from Congo. Bunche said he had told SYG he could not obtain votes in SC
                    for passage such resolution.</p>
                <closer><signed>Stevenson</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
